# Public Lists Discovery Index (`idx:public_lists`)

## Data Sourcing and Environment Migration

`idx:public_lists` (prefix `public_list:`) holds MediaCircle public List
discovery documents.

- Canonical data lives in MediaCircle Firestore (`circles/{listId}` + items).
- Documents are written by the MediaCircle backend projection pipeline via the
  authenticated write API below, and can be rebuilt from Firestore with the
  MediaCircle backfill (`make backfill-public-list-discovery-*` in the
  mediacircle repo) — the same pattern as other indices sourced from
  upstream APIs via ETL.
- The index participates fully in the standard environment-migration tooling:
  `scripts/promote_to_dev.py`, `scripts/copy_to_local.py`, and
  `scripts/bulk_clone_prefix.py` (mapped as `public_list:` →
  `idx:public_lists`), plus the management UI Promote/Copy modals.

## Document Contract

Key: `public_list:{listId}`. Payload built by `public_list_to_redis_doc()` from a
`PublicListUpsertRequest`:

- Identity: `list_id`, `mc_type` (`public_list`), `name`, `description`, `image`, `circle_type`,
  `visibility`, `circle_mode`
- Owner: `owner_id`, `owner_username` (normalized tag),
  `owner_username_display`, `owner_display_name`, `owner_photo_url`,
  `is_mediacircle_owner` ("true"/"false" tag)
- Derived search text: `search_title`, `title_compact`, `description_text`,
  `item_titles_text`
- Topics (from MediaCircle LLM classification): `topic_keywords[]` (tags),
  `topic_labels[]` (tags), `topic_summary` (text),
  `llm_classification_version`
- Items: `items[]` (full), `item_mc_ids[]`, `item_titles[]`,
  `item_title_compacts[]`, `item_types[]`, `item_count`
- Metrics (computed by MediaCircle projection, stored verbatim):
  `followers_count`, `engagement_score`, `engagement_score_version`,
  `vote_count`, `net_vote_score`, `super_up_count`
- Timestamps: `created_at` (preserved on update), `discovery_updated_at`,
  `modified_at`

## API Endpoints (`web/routes/public_lists.py`)

### `GET /api/public-lists/search` (public)

| Param | Description |
|-------|-------------|
| `q` | Free text over name/description/topic summary/item titles. `@name` routes to owner search. |
| `owner_username` | Owner username filter (prefix for >3 chars, exact otherwise) |
| `owner_id` | Exact owner id filter (deep links) |
| `topic` | Topic keyword/label tag filter OR-ed with free text |
| `item_mc_id` | Exact contained-item mc_id ("lists containing The Godfather") |
| `item_title` | Contained-item title fallback (compact tag OR text) |
| `sort` | `relevance` (default), `followers`, `engagement`, `recent`, `created` |
| `limit` / `offset` | Pagination (limit 1–50); response `total` is full match count |

**System-list rule:** MediaCircle system-owned Lists (no follow paradigm) appear
in text/topic/title results but are excluded from `followers` and `engagement`
sorts using the positive user-owned filter (`@is_mediacircle_owner:{false}`).

Browse mode (no filters) sorts by `discovery_updated_at` desc.

### `GET /api/public-lists/{list_id}` (public)

Returns the full Redis document, 404 when missing.

### Unified search integration (Search tab)

`list` is a valid indexed source for `GET /api/search`,
`GET /api/search/stream`, `GET /api/autocomplete`, and
`GET /api/autocomplete/stream` (`sources=list`), wired through
`services/search_service.py` alongside the other indexed sources. The Search tab
exposes a "📋 Lists" filter chip and renders list result cards
(`renderPublicListItem` in `web/templates/home.html`). Text queries search
name/description/topics/item titles; filter-only searches return a
freshness-ordered browse.

### Write endpoints (X-API-Key required)

- `PUT /api/public-lists/{list_id}` — upsert (path must match payload `list_id`)
- `DELETE /api/public-lists/{list_id}` — delete
- `POST /api/public-lists/index` — create `idx:public_lists` if missing

Auth: `require_public_list_write_key` in `web/auth.py`. Key source:
`PUBLIC_LISTS_API_KEY` env (falls back to `ETL_API_KEY`). Local dev bypass only
when `ENVIRONMENT=local` and not in Cloud Run. MediaCircle Firebase functions
send the key from GCP Secret Manager.

## Indexed Fields

- TEXT: `search_title` (w5, nostem), `description_text` (w2), `topic_summary`
  (w2), `item_titles_text` (nostem), `title_compact` (nostem),
  `owner_display_name`
- TAG: `list_id`, `mc_type`, `owner_id`, `owner_username`, `is_mediacircle_owner`,
  `circle_type`, `visibility`, `circle_mode`, `topic_keywords[*]`,
  `topic_labels[*]`, `item_mc_ids[*]`, `item_title_compacts[*]`, `item_types[*]`
- NUMERIC sortable: `followers_count`, `engagement_score`, `vote_count`,
  `net_vote_score`, `super_up_count`, `item_count`, `created_at`,
  `discovery_updated_at`, `modified_at`

Index is registered in `INDEX_CONFIGS` (`web/app.py`), so
`/api/index/public_lists` create/delete and the admin index-info page work
like other indices.
`ensure_public_list_index()` also applies additive schema migrations with
`FT.ALTER`; currently this backfills the `mc_type` TAG field on existing
indexes created before list documents adopted `mc_type: public_list`.

## Deployment / Rollout Order

The web service is deployed to Cloud Run (`redis-search-api-dev`) with
`make deploy-web`. Its environment is the `redis-search-dev-etl-env` secret,
which `secrets-setup` (a `deploy-web` dependency) re-uploads from
`config/etl.dev.env`.

1. Add `PUBLIC_LISTS_API_KEY=<shared key>` to `config/etl.dev.env` before
   deploying; the same value must be stored in the MediaCircle GCP Secret
   Manager secret its Firebase functions read. Until a dedicated key exists,
   writes fall back to `ETL_API_KEY`.
2. `make deploy-web` (prompts once to confirm the secrets upload).
3. `POST /api/public-lists/index` with the key. Creates `idx:public_lists`
   on a fresh environment, or applies the additive `FT.ALTER` migrations
   (e.g. `mc_type`) on an existing index.
4. Run the MediaCircle discovery backfill. Required even when the index
   already had documents: docs written before a schema addition lack the new
   JSON field (e.g. `$.mc_type`) and will not match its tag queries until
   re-written.

## Tests

- `src/core/tests/test_public_lists.py` — hermetic: document normalization,
  schema coverage, query builders, and sort validation.
- `web/tests/test_public_lists_api.py` — hermetic FastAPI TestClient: write
  auth (reject/accept/fallback), public reads, validation.
- `src/services/tests/test_public_list_service.py` — integration (skips
  without local Redis on 6380): index lifecycle, CRUD, all search modes,
  sorts + system-list exclusion, pagination, and the unified `/api/search` plus
  `/api/autocomplete` `list` source. Uses uniquely-tagged seed docs cleaned up
  after each test, so it is safe against a shared local corpus.

Run: `PYTHONPATH=src pytest src/core/tests/test_public_lists.py web/tests/test_public_lists_api.py src/services/tests/test_public_list_service.py`

